# Tailwind CSS – Installation and Setup

## 1. What is Tailwind CSS?

Tailwind CSS is a utility-first CSS framework used to design and style websites directly inside HTML using predefined utility classes.

Instead of writing separate CSS rules for every element, we can apply Tailwind classes directly to HTML elements.

### Example

Traditional CSS:

```html
<h1 class="heading">Hello World</h1>
```

```css
.heading {
    color: blue;
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: bold;
}
```

Using Tailwind CSS:

```html
<h1 class="text-blue-500 text-3xl font-bold">
    Hello World
</h1>
```

---

## 2. Features of Tailwind CSS

* Utility-first CSS framework.
* Responsive design support.
* Easy customization.
* Faster UI development.
* Reusable utility classes.
* No need to write custom CSS for every styling requirement.

---

## 3. Using Tailwind CSS Through CDN

CDN stands for Content Delivery Network.

It allows us to use Tailwind CSS in an HTML file without installing it locally.

### Step 1: Create an HTML file

Create a file named `index.html`.

### Step 2: Add the Tailwind CDN script

Add the following inside the `<head>` section:

```html
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tailwindcss/browser@4"></script>
```

### Step 3: Write HTML using Tailwind classes

Complete example:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>Tailwind CSS Demo</title>

    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tailwindcss/browser@4"></script>
</head>

<body class="bg-gray-100">

    <div class="text-center mt-10">

        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-blue-600">
            Hello Tailwind CSS!
        </h1>

        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4 text-lg">
            Learning Tailwind CSS is fun.
        </p>

        <button class="bg-blue-500 text-white px-6 py-2 rounded-lg mt-5 hover:bg-blue-700">
            Get Started
        </button>

    </div>

</body>
</html>
```

